{"title":"Career Roadmap · Sound Assistant","role":"Sound Assistant","summary":"A Sound Assistant supports sound recording, reinforcement, playback, monitoring, equipment setup, and basic audio production across live events, studios, theatre, film/video productions, television, concerts, schools, churches/cultural organizations, and digital media.","facts":{"Current degree":"BPA (Bachelor of Performing Arts)","Course":"Vocal / Instrumental Music"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Sound Assistant supports sound recording, reinforcement, playback, monitoring, equipment setup, and basic audio production across live events, studios, theatre, film/video productions, television, concerts, schools, churches/cultural organizations, and digital media."},{"type":"p","text":"For a BPA Vocal / Instrumental Music student, the musical background is particularly valuable because the student already develops:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Musical listening"},{"text":"Rhythm"},{"text":"Pitch awareness"},{"text":"Performance understanding"},{"text":"Instrument knowledge"},{"text":"Ensemble coordination"},{"text":"Stage experience"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student then adds audio technology and production skills to move from performer/musician toward professional sound production."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Setting up microphones"},{"text":"Connecting audio equipment"},{"text":"Running cables"},{"text":"Assisting with sound checks"},{"text":"Monitoring audio levels"},{"text":"Supporting mixers/engineers"},{"text":"Preparing playback systems"},{"text":"Managing recording equipment"},{"text":"Maintaining equipment"},{"text":"Troubleshooting basic audio issues"},{"text":"Supporting live performances and studio sessions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Sound Assistant generally works under the direction of a Sound Engineer, Audio Engineer, Production Sound Mixer, FOH Engineer, Studio Engineer, or Audio Supervisor, depending on the environment."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","BPA – Vocal / Instrumental Music","Music + Audio Technology Foundation","Live / Studio Audio Internship","Sound Assistant","Assistant Audio Engineer","Audio / Sound Engineer","Senior Sound Engineer","Sound Supervisor / Audio Producer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative studio pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["BPA Music","Recording Internship","Studio Assistant","Sound Assistant","Recording Engineer","Mixing Engineer","Music Producer / Audio Producer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Live-event pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Music Degree","Live Sound Intern","Sound Assistant","Monitor / FOH Assistant","Live Sound Engineer","Senior FOH / Monitor Engineer","Live Audio Supervisor"]}]},{"heading":"What a Sound Assistant Does","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Sound Assistant helps ensure that the audio system is correctly prepared and functioning."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Production Requirement","Equipment Selection","Equipment Preparation","Cable / Signal Setup","Microphone Placement","Mixer / Interface Connection","Sound Check","Level Adjustment","Monitoring","Live Recording / Performance","Troubleshooting","Equipment Breakdown","Storage & Documentation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact responsibilities vary significantly between a studio, concert, theatre, film set, television production, and event company."}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During BPA","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Music Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong musical fundamentals."},{"type":"h","text":"Vocal students"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Voice culture"},{"text":"Pitch"},{"text":"Rhythm"},{"text":"Ear training"},{"text":"Vocal technique"},{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Music theory"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Instrumental students"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Instrument technique"},{"text":"Music theory"},{"text":"Rhythm"},{"text":"Ensemble playing"},{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Ear training"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Also begin learning"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic acoustics"},{"text":"Audio terminology"},{"text":"Microphones"},{"text":"Cables"},{"text":"Speakers"},{"text":"Amplifiers"},{"text":"Signal flow"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Audio Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Start developing technical audio skills."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sound waves"},{"text":"Frequency"},{"text":"Amplitude"},{"text":"Phase"},{"text":"Decibels"},{"text":"Dynamic range"},{"text":"Analog vs digital audio"},{"text":"Sampling rate"},{"text":"Bit depth"},{"text":"Signal-to-noise ratio"},{"text":"Gain"},{"text":"Impedance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic signal chain"},{"type":"flow","items":["Microphone","Preamp","Mixer / Audio Interface","Processing","Amplifier / Powered Speaker","Speakers"]},{"type":"p","text":"For recording:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Microphone","Preamp","Audio Interface","Computer","DAW","Recorded Track"]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Audio Production","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical experience with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital Audio Workstations"},{"text":"Recording"},{"text":"Editing"},{"text":"Mixing"},{"text":"Microphone techniques"},{"text":"Live sound"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Stage setup"},{"text":"Playback"},{"text":"Audio troubleshooting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"DAWs to learn"},{"type":"p","text":"At least one professional DAW should be learned well."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pro Tools"},{"text":"Logic Pro"},{"text":"Ableton Live"},{"text":"Cubase"},{"text":"Reaper"},{"text":"FL Studio"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The specific DAW matters less than understanding professional audio workflows."}]},{"heading":"Final 